  "id": "Compound::DB01136 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Carvedilol is implicated in the interaction with Adra2c through a series of molecular and functional pathways that converge on the alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Carvedilol binds to Adra1d, which in turn participates in alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately leading to Adra2c being part of this activity. This indicates a potential functional link between Carvedilol and Adra2c, where Carvedilol may influence the activity of Adra2c through its interaction with Adra1d. The overlapping pathways highlight a possible mechanism by which Carvedilol modulates adrenergic receptor function, potentially affecting physiological processes involving Adra2c. The consistent presence of Adra1d as a mediator in multiple paths underscores its role in linking Carvedilol to Adra2c, suggesting a robust and well-defined relationship.",
